      "excerpt": "Latest boxing news covers Elif Nur Turhan\u2019s MVP signing, Terence Crawford\u2019s missed fight, and WBA title clashes. Get betting insights with odds from Bet9ja and Sportybet.",
      "body": "# Boxing News Update: Turhan Joins MVP, Crawford\u2019s Missed Fight & WBA Title Showdowns\n\nBoxing fans across Africa are buzzing with fresh developments in the sweet science as some major stories unfold this week. From Turkish lightweight world champion Elif Nur Turhan signing with Most Valuable Promotions (MVP) to Terence Crawford\u2019s promised fight against a legend that never came through, and the upcoming WBA title fights featuring the AGON duo Oumiha and Carmona, there\u2019s plenty to talk about for bettors and enthusiasts alike.\n\nIn this article, we\u2019ll break down these real, current stories, explore how African bettors can capitalize on boxing underdogs, and compare odds from popular African bookmakers like Bet9ja, Sportybet, and Betway. Plus, we\u2019ll guide you on responsible betting and share tips to make your boxing wagers smarter.\n\n---\n\n## Elif Nur Turhan Joins MVP, Unification Fight Looms\n\nAccording to BBC Boxing (2.0h ago), Turkish lightweight world champion Elif Nur Turhan has officially signed with Most Valuable Promotions (MVP). This move brings her closer to a potential unification fight with British boxer Caroline Dubois, a matchup that boxing fans have eagerly anticipated.\n\nThis signing is a significant step in the lightweight division, promising high stakes and thrilling action. African bettors should keep an eye on this developing rivalry, as unification bouts often come with intriguing betting markets and competitive odds.\n\n---\n\n## Terence Crawford\u2019s Promised Fight That Never Happened\n\nBoxingnewsonline.net (1.4h ago) reports that Terence Crawford was promised a fight against a boxing legend, but the bout never materialized. While details remain scarce, this news has stirred conversations about missed opportunities in the sport\u2019s matchmaking.\n\nFor bettors, this highlights the unpredictability of fight schedules and the importance of staying updated with official announcements before placing bets. It also opens the door for looking at emerging fighters and underdog picks who might seize the spotlight.\n\n---\n\n## AGON Duo Oumiha and Carmona Set for WBA Titles in Buenos Aires\n\nFightnews.com (3.6h ago) brings exciting news that the AGON duo, Sofiane Oumiha and Gabriel Carmona, are set to fight for WBA titles in Buenos Aires this Saturday. These title bouts are attracting global attention and offer rich betting opportunities.\n\nAfrican bettors can explore various markets here, from outright winners to method of victory and round betting. The stakes are high, and the odds are expected to reflect the competitive nature of these fights.\n\n---\n\n## Why African Bettors Love Betting on Boxing Underdogs\n\nBoxing is a sport where underdogs often shine, and African bettors have developed a keen eye for spotting upset picks. Betting on underdogs can be lucrative because odds tend to be higher, offering better returns if the less-favored fighter pulls off a surprise win.\n\nFor example, if a fighter is priced at 4.50 with Bet9ja and 4.75 with Sportybet, the potential payout for a \u20a61,000 bet could be \u20a64,500 or \u20a64,750 respectively. This difference matters when you\u2019re managing your bankroll and looking for value bets.\n\nUnderdog betting also adds excitement and engagement, especially in African markets where bettors enjoy the thrill of backing the unexpected. However, it requires careful research and understanding of fighters\u2019 form, styles, and recent performances.\n\n---\n\n## Comparing Boxing Odds Across African Bookmakers\n\nHere\u2019s a quick comparison of illustrative odds for the upcoming WBA title fights featuring Oumiha and Carmona, based on current market trends from Bet9ja and Sportybet:\n\n| Fighter          | Bet9ja Odds | Sportybet Odds |\n|------------------|-------------|----------------|\n| Sofiane Oumiha   | 1.85        | 1.90           |\n| Gabriel Carmona  | 2.10        | 2.05           |\n\nFor bettors in Nigeria (\u20a6), Kenya (KSh), Ghana (GH\u20b5), South Africa (R), and Tanzania (TSh), these odds represent a solid range to consider. Bet9ja and Sportybet both offer user-friendly platforms and popular payment methods like M-Pesa, MTN MoMo, and OPay, making deposits and withdrawals seamless.\n\n---\n\n## How to Bet on Boxing in 2026: Tips for African Bettors\n\n1. **Understand the Betting Markets:** Common markets include moneyline (outright winner), round betting (which round the fight ends), method of victory (KO, TKO, decision), and prop bets (first punch, knockdowns).\n\n2. **Follow Official News:** Keep updated with reliable sources like BBC Boxing, fightnews.com, and DAZN for fight confirmations and changes.\n\n3. **Shop for the Best Odds:** Compare odds across multiple bookmakers like Bet9ja, Sportybet, Betway, and Hollywoodbets to maximize value.\n\n4. **Manage Your Bankroll:** Set a budget for betting and avoid chasing losses. Use smaller stakes on underdogs to balance risk and reward.\n\n5. **Watch Fight Styles:** Some fighters\u2019 styles match up better against certain opponents, influencing the likelihood of an upset.\n\n---\n\n## FAQ: How to Bet on Boxing in 2026?\n\n**Q: What are the best markets to bet on boxing?**  \nA: Moneyline bets are the simplest, but round betting and method of victory offer higher odds and more excitement.\n\n**Q: Can I bet live during boxing matches?**  \nA: Yes, many African bookmakers like Bet9ja and Sportybet offer live betting with dynamic odds.\n\n**Q: How do I find the best odds?**  \nA: Use comparison tools like those on sifufinds.com to check multiple bookmakers before placing your bet.\n\n---\n\n## Responsible Gambling in Boxing Betting\n\nBetting should always be fun and controlled. African bettors are encouraged to gamble responsibly by setting limits, avoiding betting under pressure, and never wagering more than they can afford to lose. If you feel your betting is becoming problematic, seek support from local resources or gambling helplines.\n\n---\n\nBoxing in 2026 is shaping up to be an electrifying sport for African bettors, with fresh talent, title fights, and intriguing storylines like Turhan\u2019s MVP signing and Crawford\u2019s missed fight. Stay informed, compare odds, and bet smart to make the most of these opportunities.\n\nFor the latest betting comparisons and expert insights, visit https://sifufinds.com.\n\n*18+ | Bet Responsibly | T&Cs Apply*",
